---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import DocumentMeta from '@/components/DocumentMeta.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';

const sections = [
  ['scope', 'Overview'], ['data', 'Data we handle'], ['purpose', 'Purposes'], ['auth', 'Authentication'],
  ['sharing', 'Household sharing'], ['images', 'Images and OCR'], ['device', 'On-device data'],
  ['providers', 'Service providers'], ['retention', 'Retention and deletion'], ['security', 'Security'], ['contact', 'Contact and updates'],
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Privacy Policy" description="How Compri collects, uses, shares, stores, and deletes information.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Privacy policy / Draft" title="Privacy Policy" lead="This policy explains how Compri handles information based on the current app implementation." />
  <DocumentMeta lang="en" />
  <div class="content-grid">
    <nav class="content-nav" aria-label="On this page"><strong>CONTENTS</strong>{sections.map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav>
    <article class="legal-content">
      <div class="pending-box"><strong>Publication draft</strong><p>Operator details, contact information, age requirements, international transfer disclosures, and region-specific terms remain to be finalized and professionally reviewed.</p></div>
      <section id="scope"><h2>1. Overview</h2><p>Compri is an iOS app for recording product prices and comparing them across stores. This policy describes how information is handled when you use Compri. The service is currently operated by an individual; the operator’s formal name will be added before publication.</p></section>
      <section id="data"><h2>2. Data we handle</h2><h3>Shopping and sharing records you provide</h3><ul><li>Item name, emoji, and comparison unit or category</li><li>Store name</li><li>Price, quantity, unit, and record date</li><li>The display name you set for household sharing</li><li>Information needed to create, invite, and join a shared household</li></ul><h3>Account and authentication data</h3><ul><li>The user identifier issued by Supabase Auth</li><li>Anonymous authentication session data</li><li>The Apple user identifier, ID token, and authorization code used for Sign in with Apple</li></ul><div class="fact-box"><strong>Compri does not request Apple name or email scopes</strong><p>The current app does not request the full-name or email scopes and does not copy an Apple account name or email into the sharing display name. Identifying claims contained in Apple’s ID token are sent to Supabase Auth for authentication.</p></div></section>
      <section id="purpose"><h2>3. Why we use data</h2><ul><li>Create and authenticate accounts and maintain sessions</li><li>Store, sync, display, and compare shopping records</li><li>Create and manage shared households</li><li>Display limited information in widgets</li><li>Process and confirm account deletion</li><li>Respond to issues, prevent misuse, and maintain security</li></ul><p>The current app does not use data for third-party advertising or cross-app tracking.</p></section>
      <section id="auth"><h2>4. Anonymous authentication and Sign in with Apple</h2><p>Compri uses Supabase Auth to create an anonymous account. Even without a name or email, an identifier and session data are required to distinguish your cloud records. You may later link Sign in with Apple to the anonymous account.</p></section>
      <section id="sharing"><h2>5. Shared households</h2><p>A household can have up to two members. Members can see each other’s user-chosen sharing display name and can view and edit the items, stores, prices, quantities, units, and record dates stored in that household. Review what will be visible before inviting or joining another person.</p></section>
      <section id="images"><h2>6. Photos and OCR</h2><p>Compri uses Apple Vision to recognize text from a camera image or a photo you select. Recognition occurs on your device.</p><div class="fact-box"><strong>The source image is not uploaded</strong><p>The current implementation does not upload OCR images to Compri or Supabase. Values you review and save, such as a price, are stored as a cloud record.</p></div></section>
      <section id="device"><h2>7. Widgets and on-device data</h2><p>Compri stores settings, authentication sessions, and limited display snapshots on your device. Widget data is shared between the app and widget through an App Group and may temporarily be less current than the app.</p></section>
      <section id="providers"><h2>8. Service providers and data transfers</h2><h3>Supabase</h3><p>Compri uses Supabase for authentication, database storage, and server-side functions. Supabase processes identifiers, authentication data, shopping records, and household-sharing data on Compri’s behalf. See the <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="external">Supabase Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://supabase.com/legal/privacy-resources/data-residency-and-transfers-faq" rel="external">Data Residency and Transfers FAQ</a>.</p><h3>Apple</h3><p>Compri uses Apple services and operating-system features, including Sign in with Apple, the camera and photo library, Apple Vision, and WidgetKit. See <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="external">Apple’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p><p>Provider locations, contractual safeguards, and international-transfer disclosures will be verified and expanded before publication.</p></section>
      <section id="retention"><h2>9. Retention and account deletion</h2><p>Shopping records are kept while needed to provide the service or until they are deleted. You can request account deletion in the app. If Sign in with Apple is linked, Compri also revokes the Apple authorization token as part of deletion.</p><h3>Deletion completion receipt</h3><p>To confirm a completed deletion, Compri temporarily stores a receipt containing a hashed identifier rather than the raw user ID. Receipts older than 30 days are not used to confirm completion.</p><div class="pending-box"><strong>Current cleanup behavior</strong><p>There is no scheduled cleanup job. Expired receipts are physically removed opportunistically when a signed-in user next checks deletion status. This design and disclosure will be reviewed before publication.</p></div></section>
      <section id="security"><h2>10. Security</h2><p>Compri uses authentication, access controls, and Row Level Security to restrict access to data. No method of transmission or storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p></section>
      <section id="contact"><h2>11. Contact and policy changes</h2>{siteConfig.supportEmail ? <p>Contact: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a></p> : <div class="pending-box"><strong>Contact details are being prepared</strong><p>The official support email address will be added before publication.</p></div>}<p>We may update this policy when laws, the service, or our data practices change. Material changes will be clearly announced in the app or on this site.</p><p>Last updated: {siteConfig.lastUpdatedEn}</p></section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
